# 24/7 Production Deployment Guide

Your Docker stack is verified for 300 users. Here are 3 deployment options ranked by cost and reliability.

---

## Option 1: Free — Cloudflare Tunnel (Quickest)

Expose your **local machine** to the internet with zero cost. Students access via a public URL while Docker runs on your PC.

```bash
# Install cloudflared (one-time)
winget install cloudflare.cloudflared

# Authenticate 
cloudflared tunnel login

# Create a named tunnel
cloudflared tunnel create krs-exam

# Expose backend (port 4000) publicly
cloudflared tunnel route dns krs-exam exam.yourdomain.com
cloudflared tunnel run --url http://localhost:4000 krs-exam
```

| Pros | Cons |
|---|---|
| Free, no server cost | Your PC must stay ON 24/7 |
| HTTPS automatic | Latency depends on your home WiFi |
| No port forwarding needed | Not suitable for 300+ users |

> [!WARNING]
> This is a **demo/testing solution only**. Your PC sleeping or losing WiFi = exam down.

---

## Option 2: Recommended — VPS Self-Hosted (₹500-1500/month)

Deploy Docker Compose on a cloud VPS. This is the **production-grade** option.

### Providers & Pricing (for 300 users)

| Provider | Spec | Price |
|---|---|---|
| **Hetzner** (best value) | 4 vCPU, 8GB RAM, 160GB | ~₹700/mo |
| **DigitalOcean** | 4 vCPU, 8GB RAM | ~₹1400/mo |
| **AWS Lightsail** | 4 vCPU, 8GB RAM | ~₹1200/mo |
| **Oracle Cloud** | 4 ARM cores, 24GB RAM | **Free forever** |

### Deployment Steps

```bash
# 1. SSH into your VPS
ssh root@your-server-ip

# 2. Install Docker
curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sh

# 3. Clone your repo
git clone https://github.com/your-org/Flutter_test_platform.git
cd Flutter_test_platform

# 4. Create production .env
cat > .env << 'EOF'
POSTGRES_USER=examuser
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<STRONG_PASSWORD_HERE>
POSTGRES_DB=examplatform
JWT_SECRET=<RANDOM_64_CHAR_STRING>
INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY=<RANDOM_32_CHAR_STRING>
NODE_ENV=production
EOF

# 5. Launch everything
docker compose up -d

# 6. Run DB migrations
docker exec flutter_test_platform-backend-1 node src/db/migrate.js
```

### Add HTTPS with Nginx + Certbot

```bash
# Install Nginx & Certbot
apt install nginx certbot python3-certbot-nginx -y

# Configure reverse proxy (/etc/nginx/sites-available/exam)
server {
    server_name exam.yourdomain.com;
    
    location / {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:4000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
    }
    
    location /ws/ {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:7000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
    }
}

# Enable & get SSL certificate
ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/exam /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
certbot --nginx -d exam.yourdomain.com
systemctl restart nginx
```

### Auto-restart on crash

```bash
# Docker already has restart: unless-stopped
# Add a systemd watchdog for extra safety
systemctl enable docker
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Oracle Cloud Free Tier** gives you 4 ARM cores + 24GB RAM **permanently free**. This is more than enough for 300 concurrent users and is the best option if budget is zero.

---

## Option 3: Managed Cloud (₹3000+/month)

For teams that don't want to manage servers. Use **Railway**, **Render**, or **AWS ECS**.

| Platform | Setup | Cost |
|---|---|---|
| Railway | `railway up` from repo | ~₹2000/mo |
| Render | Connect GitHub, auto-deploy | ~₹3000/mo |
| AWS ECS/Fargate | Terraform/CloudFormation | ~₹4000/mo |

---

## My Recommendation

> [!TIP]
> **Go with Option 2 using Oracle Cloud Free Tier or Hetzner.**
> - Oracle = free forever with 24GB RAM (overkill for your needs)
> - Hetzner = ₹700/mo for a reliable European VPS with great perf
> 
> Both support Docker Compose out of the box. Your entire stack deploys in under 10 minutes.

## What You Need Before Deploying

1. **A domain name** (₹100-800/year from Namecheap, GoDaddy, or Cloudflare)
2. **Push your code to GitHub** so you can `git clone` on the server
3. **Generate strong secrets** for `JWT_SECRET` and `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`
4. **Build the frontend** (`npm run build`) and serve it via Nginx or embed in the backend

## Architecture on Production

```mermaid
graph LR
    Student[Student Browser] -->|HTTPS| Nginx
    Nginx -->|:4000| Backend
    Nginx -->|:7000/ws| Proctoring
    Backend -->|internal| Postgres
    Backend -->|internal| Redis
    Backend -->|internal| GradingService
    GradingService -->|internal| Judge0
    Judge0 -->|internal| Redis
```
